# ┌─ :: SECURITY + ARCHITECTURE :: What a container build may see ──────────────────────────────────
# │ Why : Every Dockerfile builds from the repository root (the services share src/Common and
# │       src/AsyncWorkflows). Whatever is in the build context can be copied into an image layer by
# │       mistake - and an image layer is published to the registry for good.
# │ How : Development secrets, key material and local build output never enter the context: a
# │       COPY of a whole project folder then cannot carry them into an image, whatever it says.
# │       The images are built from source only, so no local bin/obj/node_modules either.
# │ Ref : doc/Containers.md | OWASP A05 Security Misconfiguration | CWE-798 | CWE-538 |
# │       Threat-Model R-10
# └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ┌─ SEC ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# │ Development settings (passwords, client secrets, API keys) and key material of any kind.
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/*.jwk
**/*.password
**/keys/
**/AuditAnchors/
**/smartzipper.exclude.json

# Local build output and dependencies: the images restore and build their own.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
src/Microservices/*/BFF.Web/wwwroot/

# Not part of any image.
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
**/*.user
**/*.zip
doc/
tst/
kafka/
ps/